    "created_at": "2016-06-20T07:45:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-20T07:45:36Z",
    "body": "I think the last one is the way to go. That's also how the HTTP cache is supposed to behave (though we haven't defined that in detail yet, see https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/307).\n\nNot sure we have to cache each resource twice, but we should add a flag as to whether it was cached with credentials or without and reply as appropriate.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
